WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:57.100
<b>Dial Battle</b>

3
00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.280
Hey! That's the wrong way, Zoro!

4
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.110
We're supposed to be going west!

5
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.110
You know, west? This way!

6
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.110
Jeez, I can't believe
your sense of direction!

7
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.320
But he's going east!

8
00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.450
Aw, come on, Luffy,
use your head for something

9
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.450
besides a hat rack,
for a change.

10
00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.330
We're supposed to go
to the skull's right eye,

11
00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:14.880
so we gotta go right,
you rubber brain!

12
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.220
They've both lost their minds.

13
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.180
Why don't you go tell
those two heroes that

14
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.060
we're supposed to be heading
south before they end up lost.

15
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.100
Sure thing, Robin.

16
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.310
[LUFFY]
Hmm...

17
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.770
[CHOPPER]
Luffy! Zoro! Wait up, guys!

18
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.450
[LUFFY]
South, huh?
You should've said so sooner!

19
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:43.860
[LUFFY humming]

20
00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.330
[CHOPPER]
Luffy, that's a pretty
neat stick you got there!

21
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.860
[LUFFY laughs]
Isn't it? It's mine, though.

22
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.170
You gotta get your own!

23
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.840
[CHOPPER]
Aw... I want one.

24
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.340
Stick! Stick!

25
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.830
What's up with sticks?

26
00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.870
[CHOPPER]
You know, I thought
this forest would be scarier,

27
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.040
but so far, it's been
nice and peaceful!

28
00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.260
[laughs]

29
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.110
Hey, Chopper, you're in
a pretty good mood today!

30
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.030
Are you feeling
courageous for a change?

31
00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.110
Yep, you betcha!

32
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.290
[CHOPPER]
I feel so safe with these guys!

33
00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.780
Yeah, you're right.

34
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.110
This forest really has been
a big disappointment.

35
00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.680
Nothing but birds and trees
for two whole days!

36
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.010
Makes me wanna scream;
I'm so bored.

37
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.520
We haven't even seen
one of Eneru's priests,

38
00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.200
so I know exactly
how you feel, Chopper.

39
00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.250
Do you?

40
00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.460
[laughs

41
00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.460
Just listen to the two of you!

42
00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.040
Are you that eager for
something dangerous to happen?

43
00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.920
[laughs]

44
00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.550
[gasps]

45
00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.550
[CHOPPER]
Huh?

46
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.870
I thought I was
just imagining things!

47
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.210
Huh?

48
00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.090
– Ah! What's that?
– What in the hell?

49
00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.550
[PYTHON growls]

50
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.970
[screams]

51
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.100
[roars]

52
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.450
[USOPP]
Wind, good! Helm, good!

53
00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.280
Hmm. This is so nice. It's
just like a pleasure cruise!

54
00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.990
But we're making bad time!

55
00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.530
Navigator! Pick up the pace!

56
00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.490
[NAMI]
I'm afraid we can't,
Captain Usopp!

57
00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.310
[NAMI]
The Milky Road gets
pretty steep in places,

58
00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.140
so we have to rely on
dial power to get by!

59
00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.930
[USOPP]
Pour it on, little Crow!

60
00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.400
Sanji! You are
my official bodyguard!

61
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.720
The captain is afraid
of this creepy forest.

62
00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:47.810
Come on, for crying out loud,

63
00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.770
The only person I'm planning on
protecting is my little Nami!

64
00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.900
Hey! It's about time
for that weird knight's

65
00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.440
medicine, isn't it?

66
00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.360
Do you remember where Chopper
said he was going to put it?

67
00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.860
[GAN FALL]
Excuse me dear,
my name is Gan Fall.

68
00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.400
That's Gan Fall.

69
00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.700
[SANJI]
Oh, yeah, that's right,
I think he left it sitting

70
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.160
on a barrel down in the galley.
Can you grab it, Nami-sweet?

71
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.540
Old man?

72
00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:13.870
[GAN FALL]
Shall I tell you
a little of this land's history?

73
00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.040
[USOPP]
Hm?

74
00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.170
[WYPER]
You back again, old man?

75
00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.340
Get out. Now!

76
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.850
[CHIEF]
Enough, Wyper!
Gan Fall is here to negotiate!

77
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.350
[WYPER]
Negotiate what?

78
00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.180
No, Chief, we're through!

79
00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.440
We're not going to stand by
while two old men negotiate away

80
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.860
everything we've fought
for our whole lives!

81
00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.820
Listen, Gan Fall,
you can forget about

82
00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.610
any kind of treaty.

83
00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:48.570
If you want compromise
so badly then give it all back!

84
00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.820
For generations,
we've watched you sky people

85
00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.360
slaughter us like little pigs.

86
00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.920
Enough!

87
00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.090
And now you're saying that
you want to make peace?!

88
00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.300
Ha!

89
00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.850
I cannot give
it all back to you.

90
00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:01.930
The power of the
Upper Yard's Vearth is of

91
00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.520
the utmost importance
to every man and woman

92
00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.150
now living in Skypiea.

93
00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:10.480
All are grateful
for its many blessings.

94
00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.030
I have no right
to take that away.

95
00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.710
These people are,
after all, innocent.

96
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.720
Oh, so the sky people
are innocent, are they?

97
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.930
I guess you can call them that,
since they let you do

98
00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:25.140
their fighting for them and
never bloody their own hands!

99
00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:28.230
Maybe it's time we involved
a few "innocent" people!

100
00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.650
I won't allow that!

101
00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.990
[WYPER]
You want peace
so badly, make a sacrifice!

102
00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.040
Execute a hundred
of your own innocent people

103
00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.570
on the ancient altar and
bring us their heads!

104
00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.120
You're mad. I won't!

105
00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:46.120
[WYPER growls]
Then we're
done talking! Get lost!

106
00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.620
Or I'll take your head
as a down payment!

107
00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.380
[GAN FALL]
Wait!

108
00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.540
Wyper.

109
00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.130
Be careful when
you use my name, old man.

110
00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:02.010
[GAN FALL]
I am quite
fond of the juice made

111
00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.480
from your pumpkins.

112
00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.480
[WYPER growls]

113
00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.770
I'll kill you!

114
00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.730
[CHIEF]
Wyper, stop!

115
00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.900
Warriors! Restrain him!

116
00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.190
What is this?

117
00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.570
Kamakiri! Braham! Not you, too!

118
00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.070
[yelling]

119
00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.370
[AISA wails]

120
00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:30.540
[LAKI]
Aisa cries a lot,
doesn't she, nurse?

121
00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:34.340
[NURSE]
Yes, she always cries
when there's a disturbance

122
00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:37.590
in the village.

123
00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.510
It's Wyper, right?

124
00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.760
[WARRIOR A yells]

125
00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:43.630
[WARRIOR B grunts]

126
00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.220
[yells]

127
00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.890
There, there.
There, there, baby. Shh.

128
00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.140
I really don't know
but you have to admit,

129
00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.600
when there are
problems in the village,

130
00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.490
he's right in the
middle of them.

131
00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.830
Why? What do you
think of him, Laki?

132
00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.910
I think that he
frightens me as well.

133
00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.010
[LAKI]
He's like a demon!

134
00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.530
– [yelling]
– [AISA wailing]

135
00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.840
[gasps]

136
00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.350
[LAKI]
The Vearth!

137
00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.860
[gasps]
Wyper.

138
00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.930
I told you before,
that's Aisa's treasure,

139
00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:29.390
– you have no right to...!
– [BRAHAM] Enough!

140
00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:30.950
But, Braham...

141
00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.990
[WYPER]
We can't assume we'll
get another chance like this!

142
00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.660
I won't let this
opportunity pass!

143
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.420
If you don't think you're
up to it, stay behind!

144
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.040
I won't hold it against you.

145
00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.710
[BRAHAM]
Don't say that.
You know we're up to it.

146
00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.250
[WYPER]
Are you?

147
00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.880
Are you up to abandoning anyone
who falls during the battle?

148
00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.600
[WYPER]
If you can step over the
bodies of your dying comrades

149
00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.350
and keep fighting,
then follow me.

150
00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:10.480
Now. I swear.
Eneru's head is mine!

151
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.870
[GAN FALL]
Until six years ago, I was God.

152
00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.290
[USOPP]
Uh, did you hit
your head, old man?

153
00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.290
[yells]

154
00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.880
[GAN FALL]
As you have no doubt learned,

155
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.250
it is believed that the
Upper Yard first appeared

156
00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:34.470
in Skypiea abruptly,
a good 400 years ago.

157
00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.090
Until then, Skypiea
had always been

158
00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.140
a peaceful sky island.

159
00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.190
[GAN FALL]
Items from the
Blue Sea that were occasionally

160
00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.920
brought here by the Knock-Up
Stream were rare

161
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.970
and valuable treasures
to the sky people.

162
00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.970
Likewise, all of the
Vearth on the sky islands

163
00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.120
was brought here by
the Knock-Up Stream.

164
00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:00.040
[GAN FALL]
But a quantity of
Vearth as vast as the Upper Yard

165
00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:04.340
appearing in the sky seemed
like an unimaginable miracle.

166
00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.680
[GAN FALL]
The sky people
were understandably overjoyed

167
00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.760
and worshipped it
as holy ground.

168
00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.380
A gift from Heaven itself.

169
00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.890
[USOPP]
Hmm...

170
00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.950
[GAN FALL]
But the original
inhabitants were still on

171
00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:27.080
that Vearth and a war
erupted over its possession.

172
00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.550
Those inhabitants
were the Shandorians.

173
00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:33.220
– Then they're the guerillas?
– [GAN FALL] Mm-hmm.

174
00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.890
So you're saying the
Shandorians used to live on Jaya

175
00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.730
when it was still
in the Blue Sea?

176
00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.240
[GAN FALL]
That's right.

177
00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.530
The current blasted them into
the sky against their will.

178
00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.950
Hold on, does that mean
that you just stole the land

179
00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:45.910
that was rightfully theirs?

180
00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.370
[GAN FALL]
It does.

181
00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.370
The sky people's greed
drove them to steal

182
00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.120
the Shandorians' homeland.

183
00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.710
[GAN FALL]
And for the last 400 years,

184
00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:56.380
the war between the
Shandorians and the sky people

185
00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.380
has gone on without a break.

186
00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.510
The Shandorians are
simply trying to regain

187
00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.220
their lost home.

188
00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.590
How sad. All those lives lost.

189
00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.140
[BOTH]
Wait a second, doesn't
that make you the bad guys?!

190
00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.980
– [PIERRE growls]
– [BOTH scream]

191
00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.610
[GAN FALL]
I'm sorry,
but I'm afraid that's correct.

192
00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.400
[GAN FALL]
Oh, my medicine.

193
00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.110
Excuse me, I almost
forgot to take it.

194
00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.540
What about... Eneru.

195
00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.430
[GAN FALL grunts]

196
00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.720
Who's he? What's his story?

197
00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.730
[GAN FALL]
While I was still God,

198
00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:36.900
he appeared from
another sky island,

199
00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.900
leading a group of warriors.

200
00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.410
They dealt a heavy blow
to my Divine Squad

201
00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.160
and to the Shandorians.

202
00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.980
Then they seized control
of the Upper Yard.

203
00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.920
That was six years ago.

204
00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.580
Since then, nearly all
the Divine Squad have been

205
00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:54.000
enslaved and forced to perform
some mysterious labor.

206
00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.820
I don't know what it is.

207
00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.000
But the Shandorians
don't care who God is.

208
00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.970
They want what they've
always wanted:

209
00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.010
the return of their homeland.

210
00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:08.930
Yeah, right, if all these
Shandorians are interested in

211
00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.520
is getting their
homeland back,

212
00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.760
then why did they attack us
the minute we showed up?

213
00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.760
[GAN FALL]
The Members of the
Divine Squad sometimes steal

214
00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.180
a ship in hopes that they
might escape from Eneru.

215
00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:22.480
However, the Shandorians
still consider

216
00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.140
the Divine Squad enemies.

217
00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.400
And they will eliminate
them on sight.

218
00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.280
They must have
mistaken you for them.

219
00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:33.090
[SANJI]
Oh, of course.
That makes it all better.

220
00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.730
[GAN FALL]
One reason I became
the Sky Knight was to help

221
00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:40.600
these escapees make it safely
away to other sky islands.

222
00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.350
There is no place on the
Upper Yard that such outlaws

223
00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.560
would be able to
avoid Eneru's eye.

224
00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.060
To hear the way you tell it,

225
00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:50.270
this Eneru guy sounds like
he must be the devil himself.

226
00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.940
Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up! Shut up!

227
00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.610
For all we know, he's out
there right now listening

228
00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.550
to every word we're say
and taking notes!

229
00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:56.890
Notes! Notes! Notes!

230
00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.230
Oh, you've got to be kidding,

231
00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.730
don't tell me you've suddenly
become a convert.

232
00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.730
Hey! You heard
what the old man said.

233
00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.270
Scary!

234
00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:08.220
[GAN FALL]
The devil himself?
No, but he comes very close.

235
00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.770
[GAN FALL]
Eneru has
decreed that all outsiders,

236
00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:14.950
like yourselves, are criminals.

237
00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:17.870
What's more, he has made
the inhabitants of Skypiea

238
00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.580
responsible for leading
them to judgment.

239
00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:28.360
[GAN FALL]
This gives rise to
the islanders' sense of guilt.

240
00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:33.030
[GAN FALL]
When the people
believe they are committing

241
00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.590
a criminal act, they
become overwhelmed by it.

242
00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.640
It weakens their will.

243
00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.310
Eneru knows this
and exploits it.

244
00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:44.890
He has created a flock of
helpless lambs to rule over.

245
00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:46.390
The lives of the people are like

246
00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:50.110
playthings to him.
A devil indeed.

247
00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.120
[NAMI]
Hmm...

248
00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:56.040
When we landed
on Angel Beach,

249
00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:58.590
we thought we'd found
something like a paradise.

250
00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.650
Boy, were we wrong.

251
00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:03.300
Of all the places
that ancient City of Gold

252
00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.260
could've ended up being.
This is just our luck.

253
00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:09.140
[GAN FALL]
Oh, that's right. This city...

254
00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:12.400
You sure were excited about it.

255
00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.270
But please tell me something.

256
00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.820
What is "gold"?

257
00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.110
[STRAW HATS gasp]

258
00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.920
[LUFFY]
Run for it! It's a giant snake!

259
00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:23.600
[laughs]

260
00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:28.110
[screams]

261
00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.190
[PYTHON growls]

262
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.110
It's enormous!

263
00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:35.450
I wonder if it's another result
of the environment here.

264
00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:36.860
[CHOPPER screams]

265
00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:38.070
[LUFFY grunts]

266
00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.080
[ZORO grunts]

267
00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.870
[PYTHON growls]

268
00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.750
Okay, catfish face, it's time
for you to get filleted!

269
00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.790
[PYTHON roars]

270
00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.420
[LUFFY gasps]

271
00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.260
[CHOPPER shrieks]

272
00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.180
How in the hell
can something so big

273
00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:59.010
move so freaking fast?

274
00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.430
[PYTHON growls]

275
00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.900
[gasps]

276
00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.360
[ZORO grunts]

277
00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.200
[CHOPPER]
Ah! Acid!

278
00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:23.540
Uh, change of plan...
we're running away.

279
00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.830
Sounds good.

280
00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:28.750
[PYTHON roars]

281
00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.340
Don't let that venom touch you!

282
00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.590
It's death!

283
00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.800
[LUFFY bellows]

284
00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.600
Hey, Mister Snake!

285
00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:42.560
Over here! Follow me!

286
00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:46.020
Better hurry up!
Your dinner's getting away!

287
00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:47.810
[laughs]

288
00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.100
[CHOPPER]
Robin! Look out!

289
00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.060
[ROBIN]
Cinco Fleurs!

290
00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:56.440
Ha! Nice try!

291
00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.400
[CHOPPER]
That was awesome, Robin!

292
00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.400
– [roars]
– [CHOPPER screams]

293
00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.280
Good!

294
00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.490
I finally managed to make
my way around the back of it.

295
00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:11.910
[PYTHON slurps]

296
00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:13.540
[ZORO gulps]
Crap.

297
00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.540
[PYTHON roars]

298
00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.210
[ZORO yells]

299
00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:19.000
[CHOPPER shrieks]

300
00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:22.550
[LUFFY]
This way, whiskers! Over here!

301
00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.180
[ROBIN]
This is bad.

302
00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:38.440
I know I'm on the right path,
but where is everyone?

303
00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:41.230
Are they lost?
Should I wait for them?

304
00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:47.950
[CHOPPER sobs]

305
00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.530
I'm lost, guys! Wait for me!

306
00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.200
[ZORO]
Well, it figures,
I turn my back for one second

307
00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:55.320
and they go and get lost on me.

308
00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.570
Well, whatever, they know how
to take care of themselves.

309
00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.580
I got most of the map
memorized anyway.

310
00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.710
I go to the right.

311
00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.200
[LUFFY sighs]
Now what?

312
00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:08.620
Where did everybody go?

313
00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.290
Did they get lost?
I better keep moving.

314
00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.250
I'll catch up with them
later at the ruins.

315
00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.880
Robin said we had to go south,
and it always gets warmer

316
00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:19.340
when you go south.
So I go this way!

317
00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:24.360
[GAN FALL]
When we first met,
I acted as a soldier-for-hire

318
00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.860
to protect you, because you
Blue Sea Dwellers are unfamiliar

319
00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.910
with the ways of sky warfare.

320
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:32.620
[USOPP]
Sky warfare? What do you mean?

321
00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.910
[GAN FALL]
Now observe.

322
00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:37.450
Would someone explain
to me why we're doing this?

323
00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.950
[GAN FALL]
All will be clear.

324
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.080
Now strike that shell with all
of your might, young man.

325
00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.920
Just take it easy, Sanji!

326
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.250
If you put a hole in my deck,
I'll put enough holes in you

327
00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:48.090
to make a Swiss cheese jealous!

328
00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.250
[GAN FALL]
Hit it with all
the strength you've got!

329
00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.670
Hey, have a little respect for

330
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:55.140
other people's property
when you're a guest, old man!

331
00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.430
Well, it's your show, old timer.

332
00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.640
[USOPP]
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait!

333
00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.890
Do you have to
wind up into it like that?

334
00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.170
– [SANJI grunts]
– [gasps]

335
00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.500
[USOPP]
Whoa, that was just sad.

336
00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.250
I know I said take it easy,
but you didn't have

337
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.210
to be that pathetic.

338
00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.340
[USOPP]
You didn't even
put a ding in the barrel.

339
00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.350
No. I gave that swing
everything I had,

340
00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:23.370
like I was really trying
to put a hole in the deck.

341
00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:24.330
[USOPP]
Hey now!

342
00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.980
[SANJI]
It sounds crazy, but
it's like this shell absorbed

343
00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.230
all the force of the impact.

344
00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.120
[GAN FALL]
Now if you'd
be so good as to turn

345
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.710
the shell's holes toward the
barrel and lightly press

346
00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:37.250
the tip on the back.

347
00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:41.050
[GAN FALL]
You're familiar
with the operation

348
00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:44.010
of dial power, yes?

349
00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.840
[SANJI]
Hmm.

350
00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.720
Right here?

351
00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.450
[GAN FALL]
That, my friends,
is an Impact Dial.

352
00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.720
It absorbs any impact it
receives and then releases

353
00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:05.720
the energy when it's pressed.

354
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.430
It is frequently affixed
to the palm of the hand

355
00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:10.640
with a glove or a bandage.

356
00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.100
A direct hit from one
of these has more than

357
00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:16.480
enough power to kill
an average person easily.

358
00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:21.230
I know. Usopp?

359
00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:25.740
[USOPP sighs]
Yeah, you're right,

360
00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:27.780
that's what that butterball
priest was using!

361
00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.830
[SATORI]
I warned you didn't I?

362
00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:37.080
Impact!

363
00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:38.250
[SANJI]
Why didn't you warn us?

364
00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.920
That scared the hell
out of me, old man!

365
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.710
[GAN FALL]
I have heard
that in ancient times

366
00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.970
on other sky islands
there existed dials

367
00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.040
even more powerful
than this one.

368
00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.380
The so-called Reject Dial was
said to be capable of magnifying

369
00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.340
the energy it stored and
released ten times the power

370
00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.670
of a mere Impact Dial.

371
00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.640
But that incredible power
was a double-edged sword.

372
00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:02.290
For it threatened the
life of the attacker

373
00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:04.670
as well as his opponent.

374
00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.970
As a result,
it was very rarely used.

375
00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.440
These little shells
are that dangerous?!

376
00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:18.470
They're worse than
any weapon I know!

377
00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:20.850
Yeah, I thought dials
were supposed to be common,

378
00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.520
everyday objects.

379
00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.070
[GAN FALL]
So they are.

380
00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.240
But it seems that man has a
talent for finding deadly uses

381
00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.710
for beneficial discoveries,
no matter how mundane

382
00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:34.010
they may seem to be.
It all depends upon the user.

383
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.920
[PIERRE snores]

384
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.670
[GAN FALL]
Dials are very
useful, but when applied

385
00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:43.420
in battle, their power for
destruction can be awesome.

386
00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:46.220
For example, the Heat
Dial used for cooking

387
00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:50.480
can be placed inside a lance and
used to generate thermal energy,

388
00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:54.060
creating the deadly weapon
known as the Heat Javelin.

389
00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.980
[GAN FALL]
Or the Flame Dial,
which stores fire,

390
00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:01.150
can be placed in the mouth of
a bird, creating a creature

391
00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.220
that seems to breathe fire.

392
00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.510
[USOPP]
Yeah, Chopper
mentioned something like that.

393
00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:08.390
[NAMI]
And that's sky warfare?

394
00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:10.010
[GAN FALL]
It is.

395
00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:12.680
Blue Sea dwellers who
know nothing of Dials have

396
00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:15.230
no way of seeing
through these tricks.

397
00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.780
The same holds true for our
many types of artificial clouds.

398
00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:22.320
The Priests have forged these
into forms they can control.

399
00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:26.330
If you don't understand them,
you'll be helpless against them.

400
00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.370
Wait a sec,
then is there any truth to

401
00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.790
that mantra thing that
Tubby was talking about

402
00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:32.620
that let him predict our moves?

403
00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.230
[GAN FALL]
Yes, Mantra.

404
00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:39.230
Unfortunately, I'm afraid that
I myself am unable to use it,

405
00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:42.700
so it's rather difficult
for me to explain.

406
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:46.160
Mantra is described
as "an ability to hear"

407
00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.450
the idea is that as long
as a person lives,

408
00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:51.450
his or her body emits
its own voice.

409
00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:52.620
[SANJI]
A voice?

410
00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:55.030
[GAN FALL]
Yes. By listening to the voice,

411
00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.700
you're supposed to be able to
know your opponent's next move.

412
00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.120
With practice and training,

413
00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:04.060
you can hear these voices
over a very large area.

414
00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:08.150
The Priests can hear
over all of the Upper Yard.

415
00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:12.280
Eneru's powers extend
across this entire land.

416
00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:15.770
The exact nature of those
powers remains a mystery.

417
00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:20.280
But because of them, the people
of this land can never know

418
00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.070
a moment's ease.

419
00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:28.580
<b>God's Shrine</b>

420
00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:25.680
[ENERU]
I wonder if
they've made it down yet.

421
00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.140
[AIDE A]
Yes, lord. They are
lying in wait as we speak.

422
00:22:29.190 --> 00:22:31.990
The three Priests have
placed their Ordeals.

423
00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:36.280
And Commander Yama has taken
50 Divine Warriors with him.

424
00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:40.490
My Lord, it looks as though this
is becoming an all-out war.

425
00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:43.960
Is it really necessary
to go to such extremes?

426
00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:46.210
The Shandorians
and a few Blue Sea dwellers

427
00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:47.710
hardly seem worth it.

428
00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.420
[ENERU laughs]

429
00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:52.630
Come now, the more
players there are,

430
00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:54.530
the more fun the game.

431
00:22:54.610 --> 00:22:58.320
You, my hairy friend,
underestimate the power

432
00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:01.040
of sky warfare.

433
00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:02.830
[AIDE A]
Sky warfare, my Lord?

434
00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.370
[ENERU]
That's right.

435
00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.920
You'll see soon enough.

436
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:09.250
[laughs]

437
00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:10.710
Peel that for me, would you?

438
00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:12.210
Now, let's see.

439
00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:14.590
We have the 50 Divine
Warriors at our disposal

440
00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:19.550
plus our three surly Priests
including me that's 54.

441
00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:23.550
[ENERU]
There are 20 Shandorians
heading toward the island,

442
00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.730
the four Blue Sea
Dwellers in the forest,

443
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.220
and the four escaping
down the Milky Road.

444
00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.310
No, wait, that's only three.

445
00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:33.880
The old man can't fight anymore.

446
00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:36.200
Altogether, that makes 81.

447
00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:39.370
This battle will determine
who will be left standing.

448
00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:41.320
[laughs]

449
00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:45.000
Shall we guess how many will
remain after three hours time?

450
00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:48.710
[AIDE A]
Pardon, Lord, you wish
us to make a game out of death?

451
00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:50.550
[ENERU]
Oh, why don't you lighten up?

452
00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:51.800
You, take a guess.

453
00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.770
What? Are you
talking to me, my lord?

454
00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:56.380
But I...

455
00:23:56.470 --> 00:24:00.220
I don't know anything about it,
I'm just a humble serving girl.

456
00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:02.430
Oh, come on!
What's wrong with you people?

457
00:24:02.510 --> 00:24:06.770
You're no fun! Just take
a guess, any guess at all!

458
00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:09.150
All right, then, you try it.
Go ahead. Guess.

459
00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:10.480
[AIDE B grunts]

460
00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:14.570
Well, uh, the three
Priests are all very strong,

461
00:24:14.660 --> 00:24:17.410
of course, and those
Divine Warriors are all

462
00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:19.330
extremely powerful as well.

463
00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:22.530
[AIDE B]
I doubt many
of them will be defeated,

464
00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:25.900
but the enemy has shown
their power rivals the Priests,

465
00:24:25.970 --> 00:24:29.670
so, in three hours time, I think
30 will fall, leaving,

466
00:24:29.670 --> 00:24:34.800
let's see... 81 minus 30... leaving
51 alive, how's that?

467
00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:36.840
[laughs]

468
00:24:36.920 --> 00:24:39.630
Fifty-one, eh?
That's your best guess?

469
00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:41.720
Don't you think you're being
just a little optimistic,

470
00:24:41.800 --> 00:24:43.680
or are you just squeamish?

471
00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:46.930
I think you're underestimating
the results of this battle.

472
00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:52.180
[AIDE B]
Uh, then what do you
think, my lord, if I may ask?

473
00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:54.800
[ENERU]
Well, it's obvious
if only you'd give it

474
00:24:54.890 --> 00:24:56.220
a little thought.

475
00:24:56.310 --> 00:24:58.720
In three hours,
of the 81 fighters

476
00:24:58.810 --> 00:25:01.560
now on this island,
all that will be left are...

477
00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:03.690
[ENERU]
...five.

478
00:25:26.590 --> 00:25:27.420
What the...?

479
00:25:28.470 --> 00:25:30.010
I can't move!

480
00:25:32.310 --> 00:25:35.520
What's happening?
Why'd I stop moving?

481
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:38.230
[SHURA]
Greetings,
my Shandorian friends!

482
00:25:38.310 --> 00:25:39.230
[KAMAKIRI growls]

483
00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:40.610
[SHURA]
You're looking well.

484
00:25:40.650 --> 00:25:42.400
[BRAHAM growls]

485
00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:45.190
[SHURA]
I'm glad you
could come to my party.

486
00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:47.610
[FUZA caws]

487
00:25:47.640 --> 00:25:48.730
[SHANDORIANS]
– Shura!
– Shura!

488
00:25:48.860 --> 00:25:50.030
Now, now.

489
00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:52.200
I appreciate your
enthusiasm, but honestly,

490
00:25:52.330 --> 00:25:53.910
I know my own name!

491
00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:56.210
[laughs]

492
00:25:56.290 --> 00:25:57.460
[FUZA growls]

493
00:25:57.540 --> 00:25:59.460
[SHURA]
I'm afraid I've
got some very bad news.

494
00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:01.880
[caws]

495
00:26:01.960 --> 00:26:03.970
[SHURA]
There have been
a few changes made here

496
00:26:04.050 --> 00:26:06.800
on Upper Yard since last night.

497
00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:08.430
[KAMAKIRI growls]

498
00:26:08.510 --> 00:26:11.850
[SHURA]
Can't move, can you? Too bad.

499
00:26:11.930 --> 00:26:15.480
You only have a 3%
chance of surviving.

500
00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:18.520
[chuckles]
The Ordeal of String.

501
00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:24.980
No! Not the Ordeal of String!

502
00:26:25.630 --> 00:26:28.010
I would've warned you,
but then I thought,

503
00:26:28.090 --> 00:26:30.510
why ruin the surprise for them?

504
00:26:30.590 --> 00:26:31.800
[growls]

505
00:26:34.850 --> 00:26:35.970
[KAMAKIRI gasps]

506
00:26:39.620 --> 00:26:40.870
It's String Cloud!

507
00:26:41.540 --> 00:26:44.710
[SHURA]
Oh, very good. I'm impressed.

508
00:26:46.150 --> 00:26:48.490
[SHURA]
It's spread throughout my area.

509
00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:51.550
Too thin to be seen,
but so tough, that even

510
00:26:51.630 --> 00:26:55.010
the strongest man can't
break free once entangled.

511
00:26:56.680 --> 00:26:59.560
[SHURA]
My mighty String Cloud.

512
00:26:59.630 --> 00:27:01.760
You fools have been
wrapping yourselves up in it

513
00:27:01.850 --> 00:27:04.260
from the moment you
set foot in this forest.

514
00:27:07.710 --> 00:27:09.000
[SHURA]
Take a look around.

515
00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:10.920
Your bodies are
covered in string.

516
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:15.460
You've all become my puppets...
mere playthings at my disposal!

517
00:27:15.540 --> 00:27:18.060
[laughs]

518
00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:20.490
Yes, all of you, except for one!

519
00:27:23.730 --> 00:27:24.650
[SHURA]
Fly, Fuza!

520
00:27:24.730 --> 00:27:26.570
[FUZA caws]

521
00:27:27.250 --> 00:27:28.170
Wyper!

522
00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:34.450
[SHURA]
You can't beat me
in the air, you fool!

523
00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:37.430
[KAMAKIRI grunts]
Look out!
That's a Heat Javelin!

524
00:27:41.210 --> 00:27:44.040
– [SHURA grunts]
– [WYPER groans]

525
00:27:44.640 --> 00:27:46.980
[SHURA gasps]
Why did you throw
away your shield and weapon?

526
00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:49.550
Are you insane?

527
00:27:49.770 --> 00:27:50.940
No, he wouldn't dare.

528
00:27:51.850 --> 00:27:52.850
[WYPER growls]

529
00:27:54.770 --> 00:27:59.690
Take it. If all you want's
a shoulder, it's yours.

530
00:27:59.780 --> 00:28:01.070
[SHURA whimpers]

531
00:28:03.790 --> 00:28:06.920
An Impact Dial?
But that can't kill me!

532
00:28:07.330 --> 00:28:10.920
[WYPER chuckles]
No. Ten times that power!

533
00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:13.790
Reject Dial!

534
00:28:16.060 --> 00:28:17.520
[SHURA grunts]

535
00:28:19.310 --> 00:28:20.940
[WYPER groans]

536
00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:26.320
[FUZA caws]

537
00:28:42.130 --> 00:28:43.880
[ENERU]
And the
Upper Yard survival game

538
00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:48.920
has its first casualty.
Now only 80 remain.

539
00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:52.130
So the first battle has
ended in a stunning upset.

540
00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:53.930
Shura is finished.

541
00:28:55.220 --> 00:28:57.220
[AIDE A]
Wh-What? But how?

542
00:28:57.310 --> 00:28:59.230
[ENERU]
Like you, Shura
underestimated the power

543
00:28:59.310 --> 00:29:02.270
of sky warfare. The fool!

544
00:29:02.350 --> 00:29:04.110
[laughs]

545
00:29:04.190 --> 00:29:06.570
[AIDE B]
But surely this is a disaster!

546
00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:08.720
No Priest has been
defeated in six years,

547
00:29:08.800 --> 00:29:12.140
and now suddenly two have
fallen in as many days!

548
00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:14.590
[ENERU]
Nonsense. So they were defeated.

549
00:29:14.670 --> 00:29:16.590
So what?

550
00:29:16.670 --> 00:29:20.090
Perhaps they
lacked divine protection.

551
00:29:20.160 --> 00:29:24.500
[laughs]

552
00:29:25.700 --> 00:29:27.330
[YAMA]
Listen up, men!

553
00:29:27.330 --> 00:29:31.250
We're up against 20 Shandorians
and seven Blue Sea Dwellers.

554
00:29:32.020 --> 00:29:33.390
They pose no threat.

555
00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:36.100
We don't need to trouble
the Priests with them.

556
00:29:36.190 --> 00:29:38.940
Destroy them without mercy. Go!

557
00:29:39.020 --> 00:29:40.690
[DIVINE SOLDIERS bleat]

558
00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:42.640
<b>50 Warrior Monks
Skypiea</b>

559
00:29:45.320 --> 00:29:48.410
[WYPER]
If you can step over the
bodies of your dying comrades

560
00:29:48.500 --> 00:29:51.580
and keep fighting,
then follow me.

561
00:29:51.670 --> 00:29:55.130
Now. I swear.
Eneru's head will be mine!

562
00:29:59.290 --> 00:30:01.990
[KAMAKIRI]
Once we kill Eneru,
there will be no need for you

563
00:30:01.990 --> 00:30:05.410
to sneak around obsessing
over a single bag of Vearth.

564
00:30:12.210 --> 00:30:15.340
[KAMAKIRI]
...a single bag of Vearth.

565
00:30:18.130 --> 00:30:20.130
[FUZA caws]

566
00:30:25.550 --> 00:30:28.800
Wyper! What were you thinking?

567
00:30:28.890 --> 00:30:31.470
Just try using
that Reject Dial again!

568
00:30:31.560 --> 00:30:33.350
You'll blow your body to pieces!

569
00:30:40.060 --> 00:30:41.690
It's my body, isn't it?

570
00:30:41.770 --> 00:30:44.940
I warned you we'd have to take
risks if we wanted victory!

571
00:30:45.020 --> 00:30:46.480
We'll never beat
them if we aren't willing

572
00:30:46.560 --> 00:30:48.860
to make sacrifices! Understand?

573
00:30:54.320 --> 00:30:55.530
[gasps]

574
00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:00.080
[KAMAKIRI grunts]

575
00:31:06.620 --> 00:31:07.270
Damn fool!

576
00:31:07.270 --> 00:31:09.980
[BRAHAM]
What are you
all standing around for?

577
00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:11.650
What's that?

578
00:31:11.730 --> 00:31:13.900
We're in the middle
of enemy territory,

579
00:31:14.390 --> 00:31:15.560
so let's split up.

580
00:31:15.560 --> 00:31:17.770
There are still two Priests
out there left to deal with.

581
00:31:19.280 --> 00:31:20.950
[BRAHAM]
It looks like
they've changed the locations

582
00:31:21.020 --> 00:31:22.520
of their ordeals.

583
00:31:22.580 --> 00:31:25.790
We can't have everyone getting
caught in the same ordeal again.

584
00:31:25.810 --> 00:31:27.680
We have to be smarter than that.

585
00:31:28.200 --> 00:31:29.580
I'm going ahead!

586
00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:35.250
Hah! Fine, then.
Do whatever you want!

587
00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:37.970
[KAMAKIRI]
Just don't
forget to pray for our safety.

588
00:31:40.390 --> 00:31:43.060
Okay, men! Let's be careful!

589
00:31:43.140 --> 00:31:44.850
We'll meet at God's Shrine!

590
00:31:55.210 --> 00:31:58.670
[SHANDORIAN D groans]

591
00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:00.840
Hey, you! Are you mad?

592
00:32:01.710 --> 00:32:02.760
[DIVINE SOLDIER A]
Heso!

593
00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:03.920
[SHANDORIAN E]
A Divine Soldier!

594
00:32:04.010 --> 00:32:05.470
[DIVINE SOLDIER A ]
Correct!

595
00:32:05.550 --> 00:32:07.930
By order of almighty Eneru,
we've been commanded to purge

596
00:32:08.010 --> 00:32:10.930
his enemies from the width
and breadth of Upper Yard!

597
00:32:11.020 --> 00:32:13.390
We are lord Eneru's Elite!

598
00:32:13.480 --> 00:32:16.150
There is no place
for you to hide!

599
00:32:16.250 --> 00:32:17.660
[SHANDORIAN E growls]

600
00:32:17.750 --> 00:32:19.420
[DIVINE SOLDIER A]
We possess
the power of the Axe Dial,

601
00:32:19.500 --> 00:32:21.500
which is not found in Skypiea!

602
00:32:21.600 --> 00:32:23.350
[bleats]

603
00:32:23.670 --> 00:32:25.050
[SHANDORIAN E]
Out of my way!

604
00:32:27.020 --> 00:32:28.390
[DIVINE SOLDIER A]
Your efforts are futile!

605
00:32:28.480 --> 00:32:29.940
Your shots useless!

606
00:32:31.350 --> 00:32:32.720
[DIVINE SOLDIER A]
Axe Dial!

607
00:32:33.580 --> 00:32:35.580
Your shield won't help you!

608
00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:39.490
[SHANDORIAN E groans]

609
00:33:08.480 --> 00:33:10.020
[DIVINE SOLDIER A bleats]

610
00:33:10.680 --> 00:33:11.970
[LUFFY]
A goat?

611
00:33:11.970 --> 00:33:13.550
Was that a goat?

612
00:33:14.240 --> 00:33:16.160
– Where is it?
– [DIVINE SOLDIER A bleats]

613
00:33:18.470 --> 00:33:20.100
Here goat!

614
00:33:28.560 --> 00:33:30.020
[LUFFY]
Hmph.

615
00:33:30.120 --> 00:33:31.370
Who's this jerk?

616
00:33:31.740 --> 00:33:33.620
Man, he got me all excited!

617
00:33:33.620 --> 00:33:36.080
I thought I was gonna
get to see a goat!

618
00:33:38.400 --> 00:33:41.280
[hums]
Next verse!

619
00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:54.930
Hmm?

620
00:33:54.930 --> 00:33:57.010
Oh? It's you.

621
00:33:58.140 --> 00:34:03.140
That's right. And just
what are you doing here?

622
00:34:03.190 --> 00:34:05.490
I warned you to
leave this island.

623
00:34:06.270 --> 00:34:07.820
[LUFFY]
Shut up! I can
do whatever I want!

624
00:34:07.820 --> 00:34:09.690
[WYPER]
No, you can't.

625
00:34:09.870 --> 00:34:12.580
This island belongs
to us Shandorians.

626
00:34:12.660 --> 00:34:15.540
[LUFFY]
Oh. Really? It does?

627
00:34:15.650 --> 00:34:17.190
I thought it was God's.

628
00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:21.070
Well, then, I beg your pardon.

629
00:34:22.920 --> 00:34:23.960
[hums]
Next verse!

630
00:34:24.880 --> 00:34:25.800
[WYPER]
Hold it!

631
00:34:25.870 --> 00:34:28.250
Now what?

632
00:34:28.330 --> 00:34:32.790
[WYPER]
No. I'm through
wasting words on you.

633
00:34:32.880 --> 00:34:34.500
And I'm sick and
tired of listening to

634
00:34:34.590 --> 00:34:36.340
your idiotic babbling.

635
00:34:38.300 --> 00:34:40.840
So I'm gonna destroy you.

636
00:34:40.930 --> 00:34:42.130
I see.

637
00:34:47.640 --> 00:34:50.100
If you wanna fight,
you just have to say so.
